  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO1_UserAccess_Q07
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Why does a new user account belong in the Users container rather
    than anywhere else in the directory?
  choices:
  - Accounts elsewhere cannot sign in
  - Only the Users container supports passwords
  - It is where anyone maintaining the domain will look for it
  - Windows deletes accounts that are not in Users
  correctChoiceIndex: 2
  points: 10
  explanation: An account in Computers or the domain root works perfectly well -
    and the next technician will not find it. Predictable placement is part of the
    job.
